theory.intro:
A non-vertical line has equation $y=mx+c$. Read $c$ where the line crosses the $y$-axis, then find $m$ as $\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}$ between two points you can read off the grid.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[gray!45,very thin] (-3,-3) grid (3,3);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.2,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-3.9) -- (0,3.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-3.9,-1.6) -- (3.9,3.6);
\draw[dashed] (0,1) -- (3,1) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {run};
\draw[dashed] (3,1) -- (3,3) node[midway,right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {rise};
\fill (0,1) circle (2pt);
\fill (3,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (-0.15,1.05) {$c$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Find the equation of the line in the form $y=mx+c$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2,0)--(5,0);
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-1)--(0,6);
\path (5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[lineblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2,0.5)--(5,5.75);
\fill[black] (0,2) circle (1.8pt) (4,5) circle (1.8pt);
\path (0,2) node[left] {$(0,2)$} (4,5) node[above left] {$(4,5)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The line crosses the $y$-axis at $(0,2)$, so $c=2$. Moving left to right, the rise is $5-2=3$ and the run is $4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{ris ered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2,0)--(5,0);
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-1)--(0,6);
\path (5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[lineblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2,0.5)--(5,5.75);
\fill[black] (0,2) circle (1.8pt) (4,5) circle (1.8pt);
\path (0,2) node[left] {$(0,2)$} (4,5) node[above left] {$(4,5)$};
\draw[draw={rgb,255:red,239;green,96;blue,104},dashed] (0,2)--(4,2)--(4,5);
\path (2,2) node[below] {Run $=4$} (4,3.5) node[right] {Rise $=3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}m&=\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}\\&=\frac{3}{4}\end{aligned}$

$y=\frac{3}{4}x+2$

workedExamples.question_text:
Find the equation of the line in the form $y=mx+c$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-1.5,0)--(4,0);
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-3)--(0,6);
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,6) node[above] {$y$};
