workedExamples.solution_text:
The line passes through the origin, so $c=0$. Moving left to right, the rise is $-3$ and the run is $2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{risered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2,0)--(3.5,0);
\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-5)--(0,3);
\path (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[lineblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-1.8,2.7)--(3,-4.5);
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.8pt) (2,-3) circle (1.8pt);
\path (0,0) node[above left] {$(0,0)$} (2,-3) node[right] {$(2,-3)$};
\draw[risered,dashed] (0,0)--(2,0)--(2,-3);
\path (1,0) node[above] {Run $=2$} (2,-1.5) node[right] {Rise $=-3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}m&=\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}\\&=\frac{-3}{2}\\&=-\frac{3}{2}\end{aligned}$

$y=-\frac{3}{2}x$
